# chktex configuration for this conjecture. Run from this directory:
#
#     chktex -q -l .chktexrc statement.tex
#
# Two warnings are suppressed, checked hit by hit on 23 August 2026
# rather than assumed, with a 100% false-positive rate here:
#
#   3   "You should enclose the previous parenthesis with braces."
#       Fires on sub- and superscripts attached to a bracketed group,
#       e.g. $(S,T)$-algorithm and $d'^{1/2 - 2^{-(\ell+1)}}$, where
#       the script attaches exactly as intended.
#
#   8   "Wrong length of dash may have been used." Every hit is a
#       deliberate en dash between two names or two paired words --
#       Corrigan-Gibbs--Kogan, Diffie--Hellman, input--output -- which
#       is the correct rule and not the hyphen chktex wants.
#
#   38  "You should not use punctuation in front of quotes." Every hit
#       is the final character of a sentence quoted verbatim from the
#       source paper. The punctuation belongs to the quoted text, so it
#       stays inside the quotation marks; moving it out would misquote.
#
# Everything else stays on. As of 23 August 2026 the file is clean
# under this config and `lacheck statement.tex` is silent.

CmdLine
{
    -n3
    -n8
    -n38
}
